## Commands (from the repo root)

```
pnpm dev                    turbo dev — brings everything up
pnpm check                  lint + typecheck — run before asking for review
pnpm build | typecheck | lint:fix | format | clean
pnpm test | test:coverage | test:int | test:e2e | test:db
pnpm vitest run --project api|web <path>   run one file/dir, skip the full suite
pnpm contract               Zod → openapi.json → Kubb client
pnpm contract:consumers     which screens consume an operationId/route
pnpm contract:diff          readable pt-BR summary of an openapi.json change
pnpm skills:sync            re-link .claude/skills → .agents/skills
pnpm platform module add    install a catalog entry into this product
```

## Tripwires

Not a summary of the handbooks — the short list of rules that get broken by an agent who
never opened one. The reasoning is at the link.

- **Language** — identifiers English; comments, docstrings and user-facing errors pt-BR. Stack terms (`stream`, `cache`, `webhook`, `payload`, `outbox`) stay English. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **Comments** — default is zero; only the 4 listed exceptions. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **Docs are manuals** — mechanism, commands, the caveat that bites; reasoning and rejected alternatives only in an ADR. An edit grows a handbook ≤ 30 lines; the hook blocks more. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **No `console.*`** in `src/` (it's a lint error); back uses `LoggerFactory`. → [`back.md`](docs/arch/back.md)
- **`any` forbidden** — `unknown` + narrowing. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **`throw` is the only error path** — never `Result<T>`/`Either`. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **User-facing errors leak nothing** — no stack, SQL or path; back is RFC 7807 with `correlationId`. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **Never a second connection inside a tx** — module never injects `DRIZZLE`/`PG_POOL`; root only via `outsideTransaction()`. → [`back.md`](docs/arch/back.md)
- **Entities are immutable** — a transition returns a new instance; `Props` fields `readonly` + `Object.freeze(props)`. → [`back.md`](docs/arch/back.md) Golden Rule 29
- **One scope per change** — `feat` / `fix` / `refactor` never mix; surgical edit, not rewrite. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md), [`workflow.md`](docs/agents/workflow.md)
- **Zod is the contract truth** — changed it → `pnpm contract` and commit `openapi.json`. Never edit `generated/`. → [`back.md`](docs/arch/back.md)
- **The front always consumes Kubb output** — extend the generated schema, never retype a contract rule by hand. → [`front.md`](docs/arch/front.md)
- **A contract change is verified on the front, not in the api** — `turbo typecheck` and exercise the flow. Vite dev does not typecheck. → [`back.md`](docs/arch/back.md)
- **Contract enums have exactly one descriptor**, on the owning entity, sourced from `models/*`. → [`front.md`](docs/arch/front.md) Golden Rule 23
- **Selects show a label, never an id** — fallback is pt-BR text, never the identifier. → [`front.md`](docs/arch/front.md) Golden Rule 25
- **Transport headers are never operation parameters** — they belong to the api-client interceptor. → [`front.md`](docs/arch/front.md)
- **No barrels in the front** — deep import from the file that defines the symbol. This overrides FSD's "public API via `index`". → [`front.md`](docs/arch/front.md)
- **Kernel never imports a catalog entry** — `shared/` never imports `modules/`; entries never import each other outside `dependsOn`; extension is a kernel port, never an import. → [`docs/arch/back.md`](docs/arch/back.md)
- **Never suppress lint** — no `eslint-disable` in any form, no file-wide rule disabling. A conflict with a mandatory framework pattern is escalated to the user. → [`code-quality.md`](docs/code-quality.md)
- **Version truth is the git tag + the changelog** — `package.json` is never bumped on release; breaking changes and child migration steps live in [`template-changelog.md`](docs/dev/template-changelog.md).

## Two standing rules

**Think and work in English; answer the user in pt-BR, explaining from the business
side.** pt-BR is for user-facing replies only — thinking, subagent prompts and internal
notes stay in English. →
[`docs/agents/communication.md`](docs/agents/communication.md)

**Disk is the source of truth for what exists.** The handbooks describe the target
architecture, and this file keeps no inventory — static inventories rot. Before
referencing a module, file or package, check disk (`ls apps/api/src/modules`,
`ls packages`, the tree in `apps/web/src`).
